2. Healthcare Sector Expansion
Hospital and dental clinic applications are projected to grow at an 8.9% CAGR, with about 22,000 new installations expected by 2025. This growth stems from increased focus on occupational safety and reducing mercury exposure risks in healthcare settings.
3. Developing Market Potential
While 78% of developed nations have stringent mercury monitoring regulations, only 32% of emerging economies have implemented comparable standards. This presents a significant growth opportunity as countries in Asia, Latin America, and Africa strengthen their environmental protection frameworks.
